{"resourceIdentifier":"4963","resourceName":"Liuzhou MSW Incineration Project","description":"Liuzhou MSW Incineration Project (hereafter referred to as “the project”) is located at Liuzhou Eco-Industrial Park, Lichong Village, Liyong Town, Liujiang District, Liuzhou City, Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region, P.R.China. The Project is invested, constructed and operated by Liuzhou SUS New Energy Co., Ltd. (hereafter referred to as “the project owner”).\r\nThe purpose of the project is to treat fresh MSW with three 750t/d MSW combustion lines and utilize recovered waste heat for electricity generation. The MSW treatment system is composed of three 750t/d mechanical grate incinerators, matched with two sets of 30MW steam turbine and two sets of 30MW generator. The project actually installed two sets of 35MW steam turbine and two sets of 35MW generator. The project will process 821,250 tons [ 821,250t/d is the design value of the daily MSW intake in FSR. ] of MSW every year, and consume 330 tons of 0# light diesel as auxiliary fuel. The MSW combustion lines will generate 322,000 MWh electricity every year, of which 266,000 MWh will be exported to the South China Power Grid (SCPG). The implementation of the project will meet the requirement of local MSW harmless treatment, and significantly improve local environment. Also, the project fits the priority development sector of integrated utilization of resource and energy saving of China, and helps reduce GHG emission that would occur in baseline scenarios such as power generating by fossil-fuel fired plants and MSW treatment at landfill.","location":{"latitude":24.210013,"longitude":109.466115},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2024-03-25","endExclusive":"2024-04-25","endInclusive":"2024-04-24"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4963"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region"}]}],"participation